WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.287
PRIMARY KEY and UNIQUE are related but they are not
the same

00:00:03.313 --> 00:00:08.882
thing The primary key is the table's official row
identity and cannot

00:00:08.895 --> 00:00:13.740
be NULL A table has one primary-key constraint
although that key may

00:00:13.766 --> 00:00:19.651
contain multiple columns UNIQUE protects other
candidate keys or business

00:00:19.678 --> 00:00:26.387
rules A table can have several unique constraints
PostgreSQL

00:00:26.413 --> 00:00:30.623
also has specific behavior around NULL values in
unique constraints so do

00:00:30.637 --> 00:00:36.026
not assume a UNIQUE column behaves exactly like a
primary key In

00:00:36.039 --> 00:00:40.434
the clinic example patient ID is the primary key
while MRN remains

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:44.973
unique because duplicate medical record numbers
would still be a serious data-quality

00:00:44.999 --> 00:00:50.599
problem A useful question is if the system-generated
ID is

00:00:50.625 --> 00:00:54.915
already unique which business identifiers still need
independent protection
